            <div xml:id="d243">

                <pb facs="0394" n="300" xml:id="pg300"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890g.01/227: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-10-21T12:00:00+00:00">October 21,
                        1929—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received October 21—10:10 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>302. Department’s 277, October 19, 2 p.m. Inquiry was made last week of the
                    Foreign Office which stated the draft of Jafar Pasha’s communication had been
                    referred to Baghdad and an answer was expected momentarily. I am further assured
                    this morning that Colonial Office will appropriately press this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atherton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
